1. Sort the intervals based on their end times.
2. Iterate through sorted intervals while maintaining a counter for how many points we've already selected.
3. When we encounter a new interval, check if its start is after the last picked point. If so, add the latest value before the start of the next interval to ensure coverage.
4. Keep track of which values we’ve used to avoid reusing them unnecessarily.

